And `createUser` is async because it writes to Postgres.

```ts
async createUser(input: { name: string }) {
  await this.db.query('INSERT INTO users(name) VALUES($1)', [input.name]);
  this.cache.latest = input;
}

getLatest() {
  return this.cache.latest;
}
```

Exactly. Fix is to `await` it and make the test async:
```ts
it('creates a user and returns the name', async () => {
  const svc = new UserService(db);
  await svc.createUser({ name: 'alice' });
  const result = svc.getLatest();
  expect(result.name).toEqual('alice');
});
```

